{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>At light a murderer rises</b> — on the roads. And some say: it is like darkness. And they said: כי is like ולילה אור בעדני ואיננו (and night is light about me and it is not), for it is light literally." "<b>And at night he is like a thief</b> — this indicates about him, and likens the thief to the adulterer who does his deeds and transgressions in secret, as though he sets a covering on the face so they will not see, as though they seal the day so it will not be seen in. And what is their wage? That the Place [HaShem] will turn back to them morning like death-shadow, for He will recognize upon them terrors and set them like a thing that floats on the face of the waters, as a reed sways."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {0 "The quotation 'ויאמרו כי כמהו' introduces a biblical parallel (Job 24:13, 'ולילה אור בעדני ואיננו'); rendered as citation.", 1 "'המקום' (the Place) is a standard rabbinic divine epithet resolved per voice rules; 'וישים אותם כדבר שהוא צף' reads hyper-literally as the syntax is strained and possibly textually difficult."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:03:40.450103418Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}